  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nA cold front will moving through NE Montana early this morning.\nThere has been a few isolated thunderstorms in or near the\nforecast area during the night. Temperatures will somewhat cooler\ntoday with highs in the 80s west and lower 90s east. \n\nThe ridge moves east over the weekend, so precipitation chances \nincrease as an upper trough/low moves in. The GFS and ECMWF \nensembles have a high probability of over an inch of rain between \nSunday and Tuesday north of US 2 with lower precipitation amounts \nexpected to the south. \n\nAn airmass on the humid side is expected to move in from the east\non Sunday. Look for chances for showers and isolated strong thunderstorms\nin some areas on Sunday. SPC has a marginal risk of severe \nweather on Sunday for most of NE Montana. \n\nThe heaviest rain with this system is expected to be Sunday night\nand Monday as the surface low moves north across eastern Montana.\nThe upper low moves through the area Monday and Monday night and\nbecomes stacked with the surface low over Saskatchewan on Tuesday.\nStrong west winds are expected across the region on Tuesday. \n\nThe low moves to the east Tuesday and Wednesday and Thursday looks\ndry at this point as upper ridge moves in.\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nThere is low confidence in any shower and thunderstorm chances\ntonight with confidence increasing on Sunday to high confidence\nSunday night and Monday. \n\nThere is moderate confidence in rainfall amounts from Sunday\nthrough Tuesday.",
